## Output Format

Output exactly the nine sections above, in order, as `### 1. Primary Request and Intent` … `### 9. Optional Next Step`, under a single `## Conversation Summary` heading. Write "None" under a section with nothing to record rather than dropping it.

{% if tail_kept %}
The most recent messages are kept VERBATIM after this summary, so they are not in the conversation below. Summarize only what you are given; "Current Work" is where the conversation below stops, not the latest state.
{% endif %}

## Quality Check
Before outputting, verify:
- [ ] User messages section captures every user request (condensed, not verbatim)
- [ ] Files and Code Sections includes line-level change descriptions
- [ ] Decisions carry their rationale (not just the decision itself)
- [ ] Active working branch/state is recorded
- [ ] No fabricated changes, decisions, or user intents
- [ ] All file paths are absolute (e.g., `/src/main.py`)

## Constraints
- Keep under 5000 tokens
- Prioritize completeness for Files and Code Sections and Pending Tasks
- If you hit the token limit, truncate bottom-up by priority table above
- This summary WILL replace the conversation below — nothing in it survives outside the summary

